    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fīnītīvus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		finio (post-Aug.), rhet. and gram. t. t. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In rhetoric, <i>defining</i>, <i>explaining</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">status,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					3, 6, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">26</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					7, 3, 26</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gram. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Modus, <i>definite</i>, i. e. <i>the
			indicative</i>, <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 328</span></i>
			P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Final</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litterae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 3, § 240</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 5, § 466</span></i>
			.</div>
